akes charge as  a villain that is quite easy to relate  as king or narrow definitely aspects of  his personality I sided with and seeing  flashes of trapped ills and dolphins  really rallies you to his cause there  are some aspects that didn't like such  as the absolutely atrocious pit bull  cover of Africa by Cotto basically I  just thought oh I having a joke with our  first cuz Aquaman and Mira walk out of  the sea like like an episode of Baywatch  and this pitbull song is playing and  it's just horrendous  but anyway also Black Manta feels pretty  skipped over it sucks really sure and  he's not really elevated to be the large  threat and nemesis that he should be  these gripes are minor however and there  is a lot to love here for comic book  fans I never imagined I'd see throne of  Atlantis on the big screen like this but  James wand is a spectacular job of  bringing it to life Atlantis as a  location is vibrant fully realized and  completely dwarfed my expectations  Aquaman completely recaptured my love  for DC Comics and got me interested in a  character that I was never invested in  all of these aspects are no mean feat  and showcase just how good the film is  Aquaman is a blast from start to finish  and while it's not perfect it still had  me walking out of the cinema with a  smile on my face it scores an 8.5 out of  10 so what your thoughts on Aquaman did  you enjoy it and what do you hope to see  in the future from DC comment below and  let me know and if you enjoyed this  video and don't mind having things  ruined then make sure you check out my  spoiler talk on the film which will be  linked at the end this is a channel for  people who are super into superheroes so  if that's the kind of thing you like it  subscribe thanks again for taking the  time to watch this I've been definition  you've been the best and I'll see you  next time take care peace  [Music]  [Music]

